UPDATE companies SET description='PCS Electronics, LLC was founded in 2010 by Michael Klinginsmith in Columbia, Missouri.

The firm operates as an authorized dealer and service center for Generac, Kohler, Onan, and Magnum Energy, offering standby generators, portable generators, transfer switches, and power inverters. In addition to generator systems, PCS Electronics stocks a range of electronic components—including capacitors, resistors, relays, fuses, LEDs, and Arduino accessories—and provides preventative maintenance plans that follow NFPA 110 guidelines for transfer switch upkeep.

Customers are primarily homeowners seeking automatic standby power for medical needs or outage protection, as well as worksite and recreational users needing portable generation. The company also supports light commercial installations through its free in-home consultation and evaluation service.

PCS Electronics differentiates itself through factory-trained technicians—Kohler Service-Learning Academy, Generac factory training in Eagle, Wisconsin, and Onan HSB air-cooled certification—and over 12 years as an authorized warranty service center for Magnum Energy inverters.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Generator installation (Generac, Kohler, Onan)", "Generator service and repair", "Preventative maintenance for standby generators", "Transfer switch preventative maintenance (NFPA 110)", "Magnum Energy inverter warranty repair", "Electronic components retail (capacitors, resistors, relays, fuses, LEDs, Arduino accessories)", "Free in-home consultation and evaluation", "Standby generator sales (natural gas/propane)", "Portable generator sales and transfer switch installation", "Power conversion services"], "industries": ["Residential standby power", "Portable power generation", "Electronic components distribution", "Light commercial generator installation"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Generac generators", "Kohler generators", "Onan generators", "Magnum Energy inverters", "Transfer switches"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Authorized dealer and service center for Generac, Kohler, Onan, and Magnum Energy", "Free in-home consultation and evaluation for generator sizing", "Factory-trained technicians (Kohler, Generac, Onan certifications)", "Preventative maintenance plans compliant with NFPA 110", "Over 12 years as authorized warranty service center for Magnum Energy inverters"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2010 -> db", "Headquarters: Columbia, Missouri -> db", "Owner: Michael Klinginsmith -> /", "Authorized dealer/service center for Generac, Kohler, Onan, Magnum Energy -> /", "Specializes in power conversion services with focus on generators -> /", "Sells electronic components (capacitors, resistors, relays, fuses, LEDs, Arduino accessories) -> /", "Provides generator installation, service, preventative maintenance -> /", "Free in-home consultation and evaluation -> /", "NFPA 110 compliance for transfer switch maintenance -> /", "Over 12 years as authorized warranty service center for Magnum Energy inverters -> /", "Owner training: Kohler Service-Learning Academy, Generac factory training, Onan HSB certification -> /", "Owner associate degree in Electronic Engineering Technology -> /", "Residential standby generators, portable generators, transfer switches, inverters -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We are an authorized dealer and service center for GENERAC, KOHLER, ONAN, and MAGNUM ENERGY.", "founded_year": "2010", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pcs-electronics-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='PCX Corporation was founded in 1993 and operates from its headquarters in Clayton, North Carolina, with a dedicated manufacturing facility in nearby Knightdale. From its start, PCX focused on delivering what it calls "Predictive Profitability®" through integrated system solutions engineered and prebuilt offsite at competitive prices and shortened delivery times.

The company designs and manufactures modular data centers, prefabricated electrical skids, switchgear, and switchboards. These prebuilt modular systems range from simple skids and ISO containers to custom modules, enclosures, and E‑buildings. PCX''s engineering team uses AutoCAD 3D Inventor solid modeling, ETAP power‑system software, and RISA structural design tools to optimize layouts, claiming up to a 25% reduction in required electrical space versus customer originals. All projects are built to NEC and UL standards, and factory witness testing covers mechanical, electrical, cooling, power, and fire systems before shipment.

PCX serves data‑center operators (enterprise, colocation, edge, and hyperscale), commercial‑construction contractors, and the utility and renewable‑energy sectors worldwide. Its vendor‑neutral approach allows it to integrate best‑of‑breed components for new builds and facility expansions alike.

The firm''s stated differentiator is its "Predictive Profitability®" promise: by moving construction offsite, it aims to accelerate schedules by up to 50%, reduce costs, and mitigate risk through fixed schedules without costly change orders.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Modular data center design and manufacturing", "Prefabricated electrical skid manufacturing", "Switchgear and switchboard production", "Electrical engineering and design (AutoCAD 3D Inventor, ETAP, RISA)", "Arc flash studies", "Factory witness testing (mechanical, electrical, cooling, power, fire)", "Ground fault protection performance testing", "Rigging and set\u2011in\u2011place coordination", "Installation supervision", "Site work installation (bolting, sealing, spray testing, MES connections)", "Onsite training (system components, IOM manuals, electrical, HVAC, interlocks)"], "industries": ["Data centers (enterprise, colocation, edge, hyperscale)", "Commercial construction", "Utility and renewable energy", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["\"Predictive Profitability\u00ae\" promise: fixed schedules and costs via offsite prebuilding", "Factory witness testing of all mechanical, electrical, cooling, power, and fire systems before shipment", "Engineering optimization reducing electrical space up to 25%", "Schedule acceleration up to 50% through modular construction"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1993 -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Clayton, NC -> / and /about-us", "Knightdale Manufacturing Facility -> / and /about-us", "Hubbell brand -> / and /about-us", "Modular data centers, electrical skids, switchgear, switchboards -> / and /about-us", "Serves data centers, commercial construction, energy/utility markets -> / and /about-us", "ISO9001 certification -> db", "Engineering services with AutoCAD 3D Inventor, ETAP, RISA -> /services", "Factory witness testing -> /services", "Arc flash studies -> /services", "Installation services (rigging, supervision, site work, training) -> /services", "Predictive Profitability\u00ae promise -> /about-us", "Vendor-neutral approach -> /about-us", "Reduces electrical space up to 25% -> /services", "Accelerates schedule up to 50% -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "PCX was founded in 1993 and became recognized for Delivering Predictive Profitability\u00ae to its customers by providing integrated system solutions engineered and prebuilt offsite", "founded_year": "1993", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/pcx-corporation/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pcx-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Parts Distributing Inc. (PDI) has been a family-owned auto parts distributor in Waukesha, Wisconsin, since 1994. The company began as a 25,000-square-foot warehouse and corporate headquarters in Milwaukee, initially operating as a WD warehouse serving independent jobbers. In 1995, PDI became an official Federated Auto Parts member.

Today PDI operates four wholesale locations across southeastern Wisconsin totaling nearly 50,000 square feet, including sites in Milwaukee South, Milwaukee North, Waukesha, and Sheboygan. The company supplies brand-name replacement parts to professional independent automotive and fleet repair facilities, supported by online ordering integrations with Federated Link, Mitchell/Shop Key, NexPart, PartsTech, and RO Writer.

PDI serves repair shops throughout Fond du Lac, Kenosha, Milwaukee, Ozaukee, Racine, Sheboygan, and Waukesha counties. Its customer base consists of small independent repair businesses that rely on prompt deliveries and knowledgeable staff to minimize downtime.

The company emphasizes honest communication about product lines and service, employee empowerment, and respect for customers'' time—values shaped by its own experience as a small business. PDI traces its expansion to the 1996 acquisition of Ridge Motor Parts and Engines Stores 6161, the 2008 opening of PDI-North, and the 2013 launch of PDI-Sheboygan.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Auto parts wholesale distribution", "Delivery services to repair facilities", "Online ordering via Federated Link, Mitchell/Shop Key, NexPart, PartsTech, RO Writer", "Multi-location inventory management", "Warranty support for replacement parts"], "industries": ["Automotive repair", "Fleet repair", "Independent jobbers", "Industrial / Non-Automotive"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Prompt and efficient deliveries to repair facilities", "Outstanding customer service with experienced staff", "Honest communication about products and service", "Family-owned independence since 1994"], "facts_used": ["Family owned and operated since 1994 -> /about-us", "25,000 sq ft warehouse and corporate headquarters at 6155 Forest Home Ave, Milwaukee WI -> /about-us", "Became official Federated Auto Parts Member in 1995 -> /about-us", "Initially WD warehouse serving independent Jobbers -> /about-us", "Transitioned to model directly serving professional independent automotive repair facilities -> /about-us", "Acquired Ridge Motor Parts of Waukesha and Engines Stores 6161 in 1996 -> /about-us", "Opened PDI-North in 2008 -> /about-us", "Opened PDI-Sheboygan in 2013 -> /about-us", "Now has 4 wholesale auto parts locations (almost 50,000 sq ft total) -> /about-us", "Delivery areas: Fond du lac, Kenosha, Milwaukee, Ozaukee, Racine, Sheboygan, Waukesha -> /about-us", "Online ordering via Federated Link, Mitchell/Shop Key, NexPart, PartsTech, RO Writer -> /", "Company emphasizes honest communication, employee empowerment, respect for customers'' time -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We are a Family Owned and Operated Federated Auto Parts Distributor", "founded_year": "1994", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pdi-waukesha-federated-auto-parts' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='PECA Labs is headquartered in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania. The company was founded by a group of Carnegie Mellon University alumni, including pediatric surgeon Dr. Arush Kalra, along with Doug Bernstein and Jamie Quinterno. The trio, all recognized on Forbes 30 Under 30 lists, established the venture to develop cardiovascular implantable devices based on a proprietary polymer platform.

The company designs and manufactures a family of polymeric cardiovascular implants. Its product line includes radiopaque vascular grafts with embedded markers for noninvasive imaging, controllably expandable grafts that allow pre-implant customization and post-implant growth, anti-thrombogenic grafts with an inherent bio-inert surface, the MASA Valve polymeric pulmonary valved conduit for pediatric reconstruction, and the STEALTH transcatheter aortic valve with fully polymeric leaflets. PECA reports thousands of implants of its radiopaque graft to date.

PECA Labs serves the cardiovascular medical device market, with a focus on pediatric and adult congenital heart surgery. Its devices are used in hospital settings and clinical trials; the MASA Valve, for example, is being evaluated in an FDA early feasibility study at five U.S. sites, with the first human implant performed at Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia in June 2023.

The company’s differentiation rests on its tunable polymer platform, which enables radiopacity without added metals, controllable expansion for growth accommodation, and a bio-inert surface that does not rely on drug coatings that can wear off. The platform also allows fully polymeric leaflets that permit slimmer delivery systems for transcatheter valves.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Polymeric material platform development", "Radiopaque indicator integration", "Pre-implant graft customization (flaring/tapering)", "Post-implant controllable expansion", "Bio-inert surface engineering", "Bi-leaflet valve design", "Transcatheter delivery system design", "ISO 13485 quality management", "FDA IDE clinical trial execution"], "industries": ["Cardiovascular medical devices", "Pediatric cardiovascular surgery", "Vascular grafts", "Heart valves", "Transcatheter aortic valve replacement", "Pulmonary valve reconstruction"], "materials": ["Proprietary polymer material platform"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Thousands of implants to date (radiopaque vascular graft)", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Radiopaque indicators for advanced noninvasive visualization (first on the market)", "Controllable post-implant expansion for growth potential and stenosis relief", "Proprietary polymer platform with inherent bio-inert surface, no pharmaceutical coatings", "Fully polymeric leaflets enabling slim transcatheter delivery systems", "Bi-leaflet valve design tailored for pulmonary reconstruction anatomy"], "facts_used": ["Founded by Carnegie Mellon alumni including a pediatric surgeon -> /", "Headquartered in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania -> db", "ISO 13485 certified -> db", "Develops radiopaque vascular grafts with radiopaque indicators -> /", "Develops controllably-expandable vascular grafts with pre-implant customization and post-implant expansion -> /", "Develops polymeric anti-thrombogenic vascular grafts with inherent bio-inert surface -> /", "Develops MASA Valve polymeric pulmonary valved conduit for pediatric reconstruction -> /", "Develops STEALTH polymeric transcatheter aortic valve with fully polymeric leaflets -> /", "Thousands of implants to date for radiopaque vascular graft -> /", "MASA Valve first-in-human implant at Children''s Hospital of Philadelphia June 2023 -> /", "FDA IDE granted for MASA Valve early feasibility study April 2023 -> /", "Executive team: Doug Bernstein (CEO), Dr. Arush Kalra (CSO), Jamie Quinterno (COO) -> /", "Board members: Dr. Jeffrey Carpenter, Jeffrey O''Donnell Sr., Samuel Navarro -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "PECA Labs is revolutionizing cardiovascular implantable devices with a polymer platform and a novel design approach.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='peca-labs' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='PF Meat Company operates from its headquarters in Belton, South Carolina, with two retail butcher markets in Pendleton, South Carolina, and Toccoa, Georgia. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

The business combines retail butchery with in-house manufacturing. Its USDA-inspected smokehouse produces a line of handcrafted smoked meats including snack sticks, smoked sausages, beef jerky, coil sausage, deli ham, whole hams, Canadian bacon, pulled pork barbecue, and signature smoked and naturally cured bacon. The company also roasts its own coffee in four signature blends—light, medium, dark, and decaf—and runs PF Kitchen at the Pendleton location, serving breakfast and lunch made with locally sourced ingredients. Additionally, PF Meat Company offers whole and half beef shares sourced from its own herd and a network of partner farms across the tri-state area.

The company serves walk-in customers at its two markets, as well as customers placing special orders from the butcher counter. Its products reach consumers seeking locally raised meats, house-roasted coffee, and ready-to-eat meals, all supported by relationships with more than 100 local and regional farms and family businesses.

PF Meat Company states its purpose is to connect people back to the land and the life it produces, strengthening local agriculture and creating spaces where people gather around good food. The "Farmer Approved" ethos emphasizes that every purchase sustains the farms and small businesses that make the region unique.', certifications=ARRAY['USDA inspected']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Butchery", "Meat smoking and curing", "Coffee roasting", "Prepared food production", "Retail meat sales", "Whole and half beef shares", "Special order fulfillment"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Beef", "Pork", "Coffee beans", "Local produce"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Partnerships with over 100 local and regional farms and family businesses", "USDA-inspected smokehouse producing handcrafted smoked meats", "In-house coffee roasting with four signature blends", "PF Kitchen serving breakfast and lunch using locally sourced ingredients", "Whole and half beef shares from own herd and partner farms"], "facts_used": ["Two retail locations in Pendleton, SC and Toccoa, GA -> /", "USDA-inspected smokehouse facility -> /", "In-house coffee roasting with four signature blends -> /", "PF Kitchen serving breakfast and lunch -> /", "Partnerships with over 100 local and regional farms -> /", "Whole and half beef shares offered -> /", "Headquarters in Belton, South Carolina -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Produced in our USDA-inspected facility, using traditional smoking methods, we produce a wide variety of handcrafted products including snack sticks, smoked sausages \u201cSmokies\u201d, beef jerky, coil sausage, deli ham, whole hams, Canadian bacon, pulled pork BBQ, and our signature smoked and naturally cured bacon.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pf-meat-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='PL&E Sales, Inc. traces its roots to April 1910 when John Purser, John London, and William Edwards founded Purser, London and Edwards in Charlotte, North Carolina. The firm adopted its current name in 1986 when shareholders shortened the corporate identity to avoid sounding like a law practice. Now based on Sam Roper Drive in Charlotte, the company operates as a manufacturer''s representative across North and South Carolina.

The firm represents a portfolio of power-system manufacturers including ASCO Power Technologies, Cooper Power Systems, Federal Pacific, Gindre Copper, Bender, SENS, and TMC Transformers.

Customers span the construction, industrial, electrical, and automation sectors, with notable work in water and wastewater treatment (such as the Manchester WWTP medium-voltage paralleling switchgear installation) and healthcare facilities through Bender''s isolated power panels.

