UPDATE companies SET description='PSC Industries, Inc. traces its roots to 1954 when D. Covington Logan founded Packaging Service Corporation in Louisville, Kentucky. Logan, drawing on his industrial packaging background, aimed to serve small businesses that lacked in‑house packaging engineers. The company quickly expanded beyond that niche, and by 1962 had added a warehouse and manufacturing facility to support faster delivery. In 1987, PMC Global, Inc. acquired PSC, integrating it into a global footprint that now comprises 22 facilities across the United States, Mexico, and China.

Today PSC operates as a contract fabricator of non‑metallic materials, converting foam, rubber, fiberglass, silicone, adhesives, tapes, films, and non‑wovens into custom components. Its core processes include die cutting (rotary, laser, water‑jet, flat‑bed, and 3D contour), molding, laminating, rapid prototyping, and custom packaging, supported by engineering services for design and material selection. The company also runs testing programs for temperature, acoustics, compression, and weight properties.

PSC serves a broad industrial base, with documented customers in HVAC, appliance, automotive, office interior, aerospace, electronics, medical, and metal‑building sectors. Its capabilities pages cite automotive, appliance, HVAC, and aerospace as primary markets for die cutting, water‑jet cutting, and molding work.

The founder’s original vision — providing packaging expertise to companies without dedicated engineers — remains a differentiator, reinforced by a claim to the market’s most extensive die‑cutting equipment lineup and a quality system anchored by ISO 9001 certifications at multiple sites.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Die cutting (rotary, laser, water jet, flat bed, 3D contour)", "Molding", "Waterjet cutting", "Laminating", "Rapid prototyping", "Engineering (product design, material selection)", "Custom packaging", "Testing (temperature, acoustics, compression, weight)"], "industries": ["HVAC", "Appliance", "Automotive", "Office Interior", "Aerospace", "Electronics", "Medical", "Metal Building"], "materials": ["Foam", "Fiberglass", "Rubber", "Silicone", "Non-wovens", "Adhesives", "Tapes", "Films"], "equipment": ["Multi-station precision high speed rotary presses", "Laser rotary", "Multi-axis water jet", "Large belt press", "Mechanical & hydraulic flat bed", "3D contour cutting"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 70 years of fabricating experience across 22 facilities in the U.S., Mexico, and China", "Extensive die\u2011cutting capacity including multi\u2011station rotary presses, laser rotary, multi\u2011axis water jet, large belt press, and 3D contour cutting", "ISO 9001\u2011certified quality management at multiple locations", "In\u2011house engineering support for product design, material selection, and rapid prototyping"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1954 in Louisville, KY by D. Covington Logan -> /about", "Acquired by PMC Global, Inc. in 1987 -> /about", "22 facilities in United States, Mexico, and China -> /", "Over 70 years of fabricating experience -> /", "Core processes: die cutting, molding, water jet cutting, laminating, prototyping, custom packaging -> /capabilities", "Industries served: HVAC, Appliance, Automotive, Office Interior, Aerospace, Electronics, Medical, Metal Building -> /", "Materials: foam, fiberglass, rubber, silicone, non-wovens, adhesives, tapes, films -> /", "Equipment: multi-station precision high speed rotary presses, laser rotary, multi-axis water jet, large belt press, mechanical & hydraulic flat bed, 3D contour cutting -> /", "ISO 9001 certifications at multiple sites -> /about", "Engineering support for product design, material selection, rapid prototyping -> /capabilities", "Testing for temperature, acoustics, weight, compression -> /capabilities"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Over 70 years of fabricating experience and multiple facilities converting foam, rubber, fiberglass, adhesives, and other non-metallic materials in North America and Asia.", "founded_year": "1954", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='psc-industries-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Plastic Technologies, Inc. (PTI) was founded in 1985 by Thomas E. Brady, PhD, in Toledo, Ohio. Brady, who previously led PET bottle technology development at Owens-Illinois from 1971 to 1984, established the company after Coca-Cola engaged him to convert its iconic glass bottle to plastic. The firm is now headquartered in Holland, Ohio.

PTI provides integrated packaging innovation and material science services, including testing and analytical services, product design and development, finite element analysis and simulation, and a production lab. The company operates certified packaging performance testing laboratories in the United States and Luxembourg, accredited by APR, EPBP, and RecyClass. Its production capabilities range from single units to multi-million-unit runs, covering carbonated soft drink, hot-fill and aseptic, flexible, and thermoform packaging. PTI also offers training programs in PET technology, injection molding, and blow molding.

The company serves food and beverage, personal care, household products, pharmaceutical and medical, and chemical and industrial markets. Its client roster includes global brands such as Dr Pepper Snapple Group, Fair Oaks Farms (fairlife), and SC Johnson, as well as entrepreneurial startups. PTI maintains offices in the United States, Switzerland, and India.

PTI positions itself as a lab-to-market partner that reduces iteration cycles, cost, and waste while accelerating speed to market. The firm emphasizes root-cause problem solving, bridging design and functionality, and protecting customer intellectual property. Its founding mission stemmed from the need for independent PET expertise after Brady''s work with Coca-Cola.', certifications=ARRAY['APR','EPBP','RecyClass']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Testing and Analytical Services", "Product Design and Development", "Finite Element Analysis (FEA) and Simulation", "APR, RecyClass, and EPBP Certification Testing", "Production Lab", "Carbonated Soft Drink Packaging", "Hot-Fill and Aseptic Packaging", "Flexible Packaging", "Thermoform Packaging", "Consumer Experience Design", "Package Simulation and Predictive Modeling", "Prototyping", "Production (1 to multi-million units)", "Plant Support and Machine Startups", "Transportation Logistics Monitoring", "PET Technology Training", "Injection Mold Operator Training", "Blow Mold Operator Training"], "industries": ["Food and Beverage", "Personal Care", "Household Products", "Pharmaceutical and Medical", "Chemical and Industrial"], "materials": ["PET", "Plastics", "Recyclable Plastics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "1 to multi-million units", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Certified packaging performance testing labs in the US and Luxembourg accredited by APR, EPBP, and RecyClass", "Integrated lab-to-market services from concept to commercialization", "Production capacity from 1 to multi-million units", "Global footprint with offices in the US, Switzerland, and India", "Training and knowledge-sharing programs for PET, injection molding, and blow molding"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1985 in Toledo, Ohio by Thomas E. Brady, PhD -> /about", "Headquartered in Holland, Ohio -> db", "Services: Testing and Analytical Services, Product Design and Development, FEA and Simulation, Production Lab, packaging for carbonated soft drink, hot-fill/aseptic, flexible, thermoform -> /services", "Industries served: Food and Beverage, Personal Care, Household Products, Pharmaceutical and Medical, Chemical and Industrial -> /services", "Clients: Dr Pepper Snapple Group, Fair Oaks Farms (fairlife), SC Johnson -> /", "Certified packaging performance testing labs in US and Luxembourg accredited by APR, EPBP, RecyClass -> /", "Production capabilities: 1 to multi-million units -> /services", "Training programs: PET Technology, Injection Mold Operator, Blow Mold Operator -> /", "Global offices in US, Switzerland, India -> /about", "Coca-Cola first major client -> /about", "Thomas E. Brady background at Owens-Illinois -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our production capabilities are extensive, with the ability to produce anywhere between one and multi-million units", "founded_year": "1985", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pti-plastic-technologies-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='PTI Engineered Plastics operates from a 160,000-square-foot facility in Macomb, Michigan. The privately held company was founded in 1984 as Proto-Tech Industries, producing functional prototype molds and injection-molded samples before adopting its current name in 1987 to reflect a turnkey, mind-to-manufacturing model.

The company combines in-house toolmaking with scientific injection molding to produce plastic components and assemblies for low to higher volumes, up to 100,000 units or more annually. Its capabilities span cleanroom molding in over 10,000 square feet of ISO Class 8 space, insert and over molding, high-temperature molding, prototyping, and value-added services such as ultrasonic welding, EMI shielding, pad printing, laser marking, assembly, and packaging. A dedicated tool-transfer program helps customers revive existing tooling.

PTI serves medical, defense/aerospace, consumer, industrial, and electronic OEMs. Its quality system supports IQ/OQ/PQ process validation and PPAP submissions, and the facility includes 5,000 square feet of controlled environment for assembly and packaging.

Founded on tool making to eliminate middlemen and reduce cost and lead time, PTI emphasizes a 360-degree collaboration process with customers, from design-for-manufacturability through full-scale production. The company maintains ISO 9001, ISO 13485, MedAccred, ITAR, and FDA registrations.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 13485','MedAccred','ITAR','FDA Registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding", "In-house tooling", "Cleanroom molding (ISO Class 8)", "Insert molding", "Over molding", "High-temperature molding", "Prototyping", "Ultrasonic welding", "EMI shielding", "Pad printing", "Laser marking", "Assembly", "Packaging", "Tool transfer", "Mold design", "Design for manufacturing (DFM)", "IQ/OQ/PQ validation", "PPAP", "Scientific molding"], "industries": ["Medical", "Defense", "Aerospace", "Consumer", "Industrial", "Electronic"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Low to higher volumes, up to 100,000 units or more annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house toolmaking reduces cost and lead time", "Over 10,000 sq ft ISO Class 8 cleanroom with 350% capacity increase", "IQ/OQ/PQ validation and PPAP for medical and defense programs", "Tool transfer program with dedicated process, account, and tooling engineers", "Full-service manufacturing from DFM through production under one roof"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Macomb, Michigan -> db", "Founded: 1984 as Proto-Tech Industries -> /about-us", "Renamed to PTI Engineered Plastics: 1987 -> /about-us", "Ownership: Privately held -> /about-us", "Facility size: 160,000 sq ft -> /about-us", "Cleanroom: over 10,000 sq ft ISO Class 8 -> /about-us and /", "Controlled environment: 5,000 sq ft -> /about-us", "Volume: up to 100,000+ units annually -> /", "Certifications: ISO 9001, ISO 13485, MedAccred, ITAR, FDA Registered -> / and /about-us and /quality", "Capabilities: injection molding, in-house tooling, cleanroom molding, insert/over molding, high-temp molding, prototyping, ultrasonic welding, EMI shielding, pad printing, laser marking, assembly, packaging, tool transfer, mold design, DFM, IQ/OQ/PQ, PPAP, scientific molding -> / and /about-us", "Industries: medical, defense/aerospace, consumer, industrial, electronic -> /about-us and /", "Tool transfer program details -> /", "Quality system: IQ/OQ/PQ, PPAP, ASQ Core Tools, Six Sigma -> /quality", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "PTI Engineered Plastics is a leading American injection molder and manufacturer of plastic components and assemblies.", "founded_year": "1984", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/pti-engineered-plastics/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pti-engineered-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='PVI Manufacturing, LLC was founded in 1991 in Prairie View, Kansas, with a mission to design and manufacture high-quality, all-aluminum products that make a meaningful difference in people''s lives. Today the company operates from a nearly 200,000-square-foot facility in Fairbury, Nebraska, as a wholly owned subsidiary of Dutton-Lainson Company, a family-owned business headquartered in Hastings, Nebraska, since 1886.

The company manufactures multifold aluminum wheelchair ramps — tested to a 3X safety factor — and designs food service equipment in both stainless steel and aluminum, along with toy hauler accessories such as storage cabinets and fuel jug holders. With 100-plus employees, PVI offers custom fabrication supported by 3-D modeling and CAD capabilities, holds NSF certification for its food service line, and stocks over 95 percent of its product catalog for rapid fulfillment.

PVI serves the mobility and rehabilitation market, supplying ramps to individuals, durable medical equipment providers like Superior Mobility, and dealers nationwide. Its food service division equips restaurants such as John''s Pizza Café in St. Paul, Minnesota, and institutions like Freestate School in Lawrence, Kansas. The toy hauler line targets recreational vehicle owners and garage organizers.

