UPDATE companies SET description='Paperless Parts is headquartered in Boston, Massachusetts. The company traces its roots to 2001 when Jay Jacobs founded RAPID Manufacturing, which grew into the world''s largest prototype sheet metal and second-largest prototype CNC machining business.

The company provides a cloud-based quoting and estimating platform built for custom manufacturers. Its software automates geometry-driven costing, detects manufacturability issues, supports multi-component nesting, and applies customizable pricing logic across processes including sheet metal fabrication, multi-axis CNC machining, Swiss screw machining, and additive manufacturing. The platform handles digital quoting, CRM, and real-time analytics, with customers collectively sending roughly 45,000 quotes per week and quoting over $35 billion in parts during 2025.

Paperless Parts serves job shops and contract manufacturers of all sizes, from one-person operations to facilities running $100 million contracts. Its customer base of more than 800 manufacturers spans industries such as aerospace, automotive, and medical, with documented deployments at companies including Quality Fabricators Inc., Jax Precision, Special Products & Mfg. (SPM), and KMM Group.

The founders built the platform because they believed software should adapt to a shop''s workflow rather than force a one-size-fits-all process. The system is ITAR registered, hosted on AWS GovCloud with 100 percent U.S.-based support, and meets FedRAMP Moderate Equivalent and CMMC Level 2 assessment-ready standards, addressing the security requirements of defense and regulated-industry customers.', certifications=ARRAY['ITAR registered','FedRAMP Moderate Equivalent','CMMC Level 2 Assessment-Ready']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Automated quoting and estimating", "Geometry-driven costing", "Design for manufacturability (DFM) analysis", "Multi-component nesting", "Customizable pricing logic", "Digital quoting and CRM", "Real-time analytics", "Sheet metal fabrication quoting", "CNC machining (multi-axis milling/turning) quoting", "Swiss screw machining quoting", "Additive manufacturing (3D printing) quoting"], "industries": ["Custom manufacturing", "Job shops", "Contract manufacturing", "Aerospace", "Automotive", "Medical"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ITAR registered with 100% U.S.-based administrators and support", "Hosted on AWS GovCloud with nightly backups and full disaster recovery", "FedRAMP Moderate Equivalent and CMMC Level 2 Assessment-Ready", "Geometry-driven costing engine with automated design-for-manufacturability warnings", "In-app multi-component nesting and customizable pricing logic"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Boston, Massachusetts -> db", "Jay Jacobs founded RAPID Manufacturing in 2001 -> /about", "Paperless Parts founded to extend RAPID''s technology to other manufacturers -> /about", "Jason Ray is Co-Founder & CEO -> /quality", "800+ customers worldwide -> /about", "45,000 quotes sent per week -> /about", "$35B parts quoted in 2025 -> /about", "ITAR registered -> /", "FedRAMP Moderate Equivalent -> /", "CMMC Level 2 Assessment-Ready -> /", "100% US-based system administrators and support -> /", "Hosted on AWS US GovCloud -> /", "Serves job shops and contract manufacturers -> /about", "Customer examples: Quality Fabricators Inc., Jax Precision, SPM, KMM Group -> /about, /quality", "Industries: aerospace, automotive, medical -> /quality", "Software features: geometry-driven costing, DFM warnings, nesting, pricing logic, digital quotes, CRM, analytics -> /, /quality"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Paperless Parts is the #1 estimating and quoting software in manufacturing", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='paperless-parts' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Paradise Power Company, Inc. (PPC Solar) was founded in 1979 by Michael Weinman in Taos, New Mexico, to meet the demand for solar technology supporting the off-grid lifestyle common in northern New Mexico. The family-owned business passed to his son, Daniel Weinman, in 1993, and remains locally operated with headquarters in Taos and a fully staffed office and warehouse in Albuquerque.

The company provides turnkey engineering, procurement, and construction of solar photovoltaic, battery energy storage, and electric vehicle charging systems for residential, commercial, school, government, and utility clients. Since its founding, PPC has installed more than 30 megawatts of photovoltaic capacity and over 200 EV charging stations across New Mexico and Colorado, managing projects from design through long-term maintenance.

Customers include the Northern New Mexico School Employees Federal Credit Union in Santa Fe, Taos Mountain Builders, San Miguel County, Bartee Ranch, Angel Fire Family Dentistry, Eastern New Mexico University, and state agencies such as the New Mexico General Services Department and the New Mexico Department of Transportation. The firm also serves commercial clients like Taos Spa and Siemens.

