UPDATE companies SET description='Patience Metal Fab operates from Brooklyn Center, Minnesota, and was founded in 2012. The shop began as a team of automotive enthusiasts and fabrication specialists focused on turning customer concepts into finished vehicles, earning a reputation across the Midwest as the “Last Stop Fab Shop” for completing projects other shops could not.

The company provides a range of fabrication services including MIG and TIG welding of aluminum, steel, and stainless steel; lathe and mill machining; tube bending; sheet-metal forming with brakes, bead rollers, slip rolls, and an English wheel; and composite and lightweight-alloy work. In-house capabilities extend to 3D scanning, CFD simulation, certified roll-cage construction, custom chassis fabrication, exhaust systems, forced-induction plumbing, engine swaps, and aero design. The shop reports more than 20,000 hours of cage and chassis fabrication experience.

Patience Metal Fab serves the motorsports and street-rod segments, working with individual builders, race teams, and restoration projects. Past projects include a NASA AIX/SU Mustang, a Camaro ZL1 LE built for Nick Plocienik, a Volkswagen MK2 VR6 nicknamed “Waskly,” and a 1950s Ford F1 restomod known as “Gramps.”

The business was started to address a gap in the market for a fabrication shop that could handle unique, difficult builds and see them through to completion, a mission reflected in its “Last Stop Fab Shop” moniker and its emphasis on 3D scanning and simulation to validate designs before cutting metal.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["MIG welding", "TIG welding", "Aluminum welding", "Steel welding", "Stainless steel welding", "Lathe machining", "Mill machining", "Tube bending", "Sheet metal brake forming", "Bead rolling", "Slip roll forming", "English wheel forming", "Dimple die forming", "Chassis fabrication", "Certified roll cage fabrication", "Custom tube work", "Narrowed rear end fabrication", "Exhaust fabrication", "Forced induction plumbing fabrication", "Custom engine swaps", "Custom aero design and implementation", "3D scanning", "CFD simulation", "Composite and lightweight alloy fabrication", "Custom mounting for trailer loading"], "industries": ["Motorsports", "Street Rod", "Automotive"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Steel", "Stainless Steel", "Composite", "Lightweight alloy"], "equipment": ["Lathe", "Mill", "Tube bender", "Sheet metal brake", "Bead roller", "Slip roll", "English wheel", "Dimple dies", "3D scanner"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["20,000+ hours of cage and chassis fabrication experience", "Known as the ''Last Stop Fab Shop'' in the Midwest for completing difficult projects", "In-house 3D scanning and CFD simulation for design validation", "Certified roll-cage fabrication", "Composite and lightweight-alloy fabrication capabilities"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Brooklyn Center, Minnesota -> db", "Founded: 2012 -> db", "20,000+ hours of cage/chassis fabrication -> /", "75 years of fabrication experience -> /", "53 years of mechanic experience -> /", "14 years in business -> /", "Known as ''Last Stop Fab Shop'' in the Midwest -> /", "Services: MIG/TIG welding, lathe and mill machinin