UPDATE companies SET description='Peak Manufacturing and Fulfillment was founded in 2015 in Englewood, Colorado. The company draws on nearly four decades of manufacturing and assembly experience, operating as an integrated production and fulfillment enterprise.

The facility runs a standardized fleet of Nissei injection molding presses—hydraulic, electric, and hybrid—ranging from 22 to 720 tons, supported by robotics, automation, and secondary screws for clear polymer production. Personnel are trained in scientific decoupled molding and work with all thermoplastic materials. Beyond molding, Peak provides design and engineering consultation, prototyping, assembly and kitting, custom packaging, warehousing with 24/7 inventory visibility, and fulfillment and shipping services that leverage combined purchasing power for discounted carrier rates.

Peak serves medical device manufacturers, consumer and industrial product companies, and shelf-stable food brands. Its customers range from startups needing warehousing and automated shipping to mid-sized and large businesses seeking a single-source partner for design, production, packaging, and distribution.

The company emphasizes its "complex circular structure" that consolidates design, development, and distribution under one roof. Affiliation with sister company Caroba Plastics and packaging supplier Pozzetta Specialty Supplies extends purchasing power and packaging capabilities. Peak’s stated mission is to understand each client’s logistical needs and deliver simple, scalable solutions.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Thermoplastic injection molding", "Assembly and kitting", "Packaging design and supply", "Warehousing and inventory management", "Order fulfillment and shipping", "Product design and engineering consultation", "Prototyping", "Material selection", "Scientific decoupled molding", "Robotics and automation integration", "Secondary operations for clear polymers", "Custom packaging design", "Supply chain management"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Consumer products", "Industrial products", "Shelf-stable foods"], "materials": ["Thermoplastics"], "equipment": ["Nissei hydraulic injection molding presses", "Nissei electric injection molding presses", "Nissei hybrid injection molding presses", "Robotics", "Automation systems", "Secondary screws for clear polymer production"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Integrated design, manufacturing, assembly, packaging, warehousing, fulfillment, and shipping in one facility", "Standardized fleet of Nissei injection molding presses (22\u2013720 tons) with robotics and automation", "Scientific decoupled molding trained personnel", "Exclusive discounted shipping rates through combined purchasing power with affiliated companies", "24/7 order tracking visibility via web-based portal"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2015 -> db", "Headquarters Englewood, Colorado -> db and homepage (address)", "Nearly 40 years of manufacturing and assembly experience -> homepage", "Integrated manufacturing and fulfillment enterprise -> homepage", "Complex circular structure consolid