illment' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Pearson Medical Technologies LLC was founded in 1996 in Alexandria, Louisiana. The company has spent over three decades developing pharmacy automation technology, marking its 30th anniversary with a focus on unit dose packaging and barcode labeling systems.

The company designs and manufactures its own line of pharmacy automation equipment, including the m:Print® v4 barcode labeling software with 1-Click Print® Technology, the intelliCount® Automated Universal Feeder, and the Fillin Station™ Automated Feeder. All products are produced in the United States. The software automates drug information capture, label template selection, beyond-use date calculation, and packaging initiation, while the feeders operate without custom canisters for unattended or high-speed tabletop packaging.

Pearson Medical Technologies serves pharmacies, hospitals, long-term care facilities, and retail pharmacies across the United States, with installations reported in Florida, Pennsylvania, Georgia, North Carolina, Ohio, New York, and Illinois, as well as internationally. Its solutions target medication packaging, dispensing accuracy, and regulatory compliance such as the Drug Supply Chain Security Act (DSCSA).

The company differentiates itself by offering two non-canister automated feeder options, a feature it claims is unique in the market. Its 1-Click Print® Technology eliminates manual keyboarding for most packaging runs, and the company reports a 99.9% dispensing accuracy rate across facilities. Patient safety and DSCSA compliance are cited as core drivers behind its product development.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Unit dose packaging", "Barcode labeling", "Medication packaging", "Automated feeding (canister-free)", "DSCSA compliance labeling", "Beyond Use Date (BUD) calculation", "Rules-based workflow automation", "Pharmacy workflow optimization", "Software development for pharmacy automation"], "industries": ["Pharmacy", "Hospital", "Long-term care", "Retail pharmacy", "Healthcare"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["m:Print\u00ae v4 Bar Code Labeling Software", "intelliCount\u00ae Automated Universal Feeder", "Fillin Station\u2122 Automated Feeder"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Only company offering two non-canister automated feeder options", "1-Click Print\u00ae Technology eliminates keyboarding for most packaging runs", "m:Print\u00ae v4 software supports DSCSA compliance and serialized unit dose packaging", "99.9% dispensing accuracy rate across facilities", "All products manufactured in the USA"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1996 -> db, /", "Headquarters Alexandria, Louisiana -> db", "Manufactures pharmacy automation technology -> /", "Products: m:Print v4, intelliCount, Fillin Station -> /", "Serves pharmacies, hospitals, long-term care, retail pharmacies nationwide -> /", "99.9% dispensing accuracy rate -> /", "Only company offering two non-canister automated feeder options -> /", "1-Click Print Technology eliminates keyboarding -> /", "All products manufactured in USA -> /", "DSCSA compliance support -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Every product is proudly manufactured by us in the USA", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/pearson-medical-technologies/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pearson-medical-technologies-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Pelham Plastics Inc operates from Pelham, New Hampshire. The company does not disclose its founding year or ownership structure, but its capabilities page describes its origins as a customer-centric venture built on an "open-door philosophy" emphasizing teamwork and one-on-one relationships.

The company provides full injection and insert molding for thermoplastic materials, along with over-molding, RF thermoforming, and embedded marker band integration. Its single-source facility includes a tool room capable of producing single-cavity prototype molds up to multi-cavity Class 101 production tooling, plus 3D printing, mold flow analysis, and assembly services performed in white room environments. Engineering support spans R&D, design assistance, and scientific molding principles backed by lean manufacturing initiatives such as 6S and Kaizen.

Pelham Plastics serves the medical device industry, producing components and assemblies that are inserted into the human body. A 2020 Plastics News article highlighted the company''s solution for a medical marker problem, and its quality page notes that many products are destined for implantation. The firm also partners with community organizations such as the Humane Society for Greater Nashua.

