y: open-door, customer-centric -> /capabilities", "Single-source facility description -> /capabilities"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Full injection and insert molding for thermo plastic materials.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pelham-plastics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Peliton Plastics was founded in 1996 by Robert McKinnon in Valdosta, Georgia. The company remains family-owned and operates from a 35,000-square-foot facility in South Georgia, where it has built a full-service plastic injection molding and contract manufacturing operation over nearly three decades.

The shop runs 55- to 650-ton molding machines capable of shot sizes from 0.001 to 5 pounds, processing a wide range of thermoplastics and engineered resins. Beyond molding, Peliton provides insert molding, overmolding, in-house mold making and repair (including EDM and mold texturing), CNC milling, turning, and grinding, as well as pad and screen printing on plastics, vinyl, metal, and glass. Assembly services include ultrasonic welding, kitting, packaging, and shipping, while a 3D printing capability supports prototyping and low-volume runs.

Customers span medical devices, agriculture, automotive, kitchen products, toys, pest control, industrial components, electronic enclosures, promotional products, home and office goods, and tools. The company also works directly with inventors, offering NDA-protected development from concept to market-ready product.

Peliton emphasizes domestic production as a differentiator: all tooling, molding, finishing, and printing occur under one roof, eliminating overseas shipping delays and protecting intellectual property. The team specializes in reshoring projects, offering fast partial-order shipments and direct access to the production floor for real-time communication.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom plastic injection molding", "Insert molding", "Overmolding", "Mold making and repair", "Mold texturing", "EDM (electrical discharge machining)", "Assembly and fulfillment", "Ultrasonic welding", "Second operations", "Kitting", "Packaging and shipping", "Pad printing", "Screen printing", "CNC milling", "CNC turning", "Grinding", "3D prototyping", "Project management"], "industries": ["Medical Devices", "Agriculture", "Automotive Parts", "Kitchen Products", "Toys", "Pest Control", "Industrial Components", "Electronic Enclosures", "Promotional Products", "Home & Office", "Tools"], "materials": ["thermoplastics", "engineered resins"], "equipment": ["55-650 ton injection molding machines", "CNC milling machines", "CNC lathes", "Grinding machines", "EDM machines", "3D printers"], "volume": "Low to high volume", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house tooling, mold repair, and pad printing under one roof", "Reshoring and re-tooling expertise with fast partial-order shipping", "Direct communication with the production team, no overseas intermediaries", "IP protection with NDA-friendly process for inventors", "Family-owned since 1996 with 35,000 sq. ft. facility in Valdosta, GA"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1996 by Robert McKinnon -> db", "Family-owned since 1996 -> /", "35,000 sq. ft. facility in Valdosta, GA -> /", "55-650 ton injection molding machines -> /", "Shot sizes 0.001 to 5 lb -> /", "In-house tooling, mold repair, and pad printing -> /", "Industries served: Medical Devices, Agriculture, Automotive Parts, Kitchen Products, Toys, 