UPDATE companies SET description='The Woodwright Shop operates from Covington, Louisiana, where husband-and-wife team Tom and Leah Edmonds have led the business for over two decades. The Edmonds built the shop around a shared dedication to architectural millwork, growing a team of designers and craftsmen that now includes ten members.

The shop produces historic reproduction and custom architectural millwork for both restoration projects and new construction. Its capabilities include hand-turned newel posts, balusters, and columns up to 14 feet long, custom handrail fittings such as tangent curves, and exact moulding replication from customer-supplied samples. All turnings are done by hand, and the team works from photographs or original designs to create one-off pieces.

Clients range from public institutions to hospitality and residential owners. The portfolio lists work at the Louisiana Governor''s Mansion, the Historic Cabildo, Le Petit Théâtre, the Left Pontalba, Hotel Peter & Paul, the French Market Inn, the Frenchmen Hotel, and numerous other historic properties across New Orleans.

The Edmonds emphasize constant communication throughout each project and a willingness to become an extension of the client''s team. They position the shop as a partner that can translate a photo or a fragment of original moulding into a finished component, with a focus on durability and detail.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Historic reproduction millwork", "Custom architectural millwork", "Custom handrail fabrication", "Hand turning (newel posts, balusters, columns)", "Moulding reproduction from samples", "Custom design from photos or ideas", "Millwork for historic restoration", "Millwork for new construction"], "industries": ["Historic preservation", "Hospitality", "Government", "Commercial construction", "Residential construction"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Hand-turned posts, balusters, and columns up to 14 feet long", "Exact moulding reproduction from customer samples", "Custom handrail fittings including tangent curves", "Dedicated team of designers and craftsmen", "Constant client communication through project completion"], "facts_used": ["Location: Covington, LA (306 E Lockwood St) -> /", "Founders: Tom and Leah Edmonds, husband-wife team -> /about", "Team size: 10 designers and craftsmen listed -> /about", "Notable projects: Louisiana Governor''s Mansion, Historic Cabildo, Le Petit Theatre, Left Pontalba, Hotel Peter & Paul, French Market Inn, Frenchmen Hotel -> /about", "Capabilities: hand-turned posts up to 14'', custom handrail fittings, moulding reproduction from samples -> /about", "Services: historic reproduction and custom millwork for restoration and new builds -> /", "Communication: constant communication until job done -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Historic Reproduction & Truly Custom Millwork", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "10", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='period-millworks-the-woodwright-shop' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='PharoPLAST Injection Molding operates from Cleveland, Ohio, where it was founded in 1972 as Innovations in Plastic with a single injection molding machine in a small rented space. The company transitioned to its current name in 2022 when Christopher Miedza, a longtime tooling and design partner, assumed ownership. Today it remains a family-owned business led by Christopher and his son Simon Miedza, who directs sales and regional growth across the Midwest.

The shop provides engineering-led thermoplastic injection molding backed by in-house product design, DFM/DFA guidance, tooling sourcing, refurbishment, and transfer services. It also offers reshoring support, additive prototyping, and secondary operations such as assembly, welding, decoration, and packaging. PharoPLAST emphasizes flexible volume production with no minimum order quantity and advertises 24-hour lead times once tooling is on site.

Primary customers are OEMs and manufacturers in industrial, electrical, and equipment markets. Long-standing accounts include Parker Hannifin, Eaton, and Steris. The company focuses on the Midwest corridor — Ohio, Pennsylvania, Michigan, Kentucky, West Virginia — and works with businesses of all sizes, maintaining a dedicated small-project division for runs as low as 50 parts.

PharoPLAST was built on the premise that most molding problems originate before a part reaches the press. By integrating engineering early — catching warpage, sink, and assembly conflicts before steel is cut — the company aims to eliminate rework, compress launch timelines, and give customers transparent tooling ownership and direct access to decision-makers.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Thermoplastic injection molding", "Product design and engineering", "DFM/DFA analysis", "Tooling design and transfer", "Tool refurbishment and rescue", "Reshoring and tool transfer management", "Additive manufacturing (prototyping)", "Assembly and secondary operations", "Plastic welding", "Decorating and packaging"], "industries": ["Industrial", "Electrical", "Equipment", "Original equipment manufacturers (OEMs)"], "materials": ["Thermoplastics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Low volume to large quantities", "lead_time": "24 hours", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No minimum order quantity (MOQ)", "24-hour lead times after tooling arrives", "Engineering-led design support before tooling is cut", "Transparent tooling ownership and pricing", "Family-owned accountability with direct access to leadership"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1972 as Innovations in Plastic -> /about", "Ownership transitioned to Christopher Miedza in 2022 -> /about", "Family-owned business led by Christopher and Simon Miedza -> /about", "Headquarters Cleveland, Ohio -> /", "Services: Thermoplastic Injection Molding, Product Design & Engineering, Tooling & Tool Transfers, Reshoring & Retooling, Additive & Secondary Services -> /services", "Industries: Industrial, Electrical, Equipment -> /", "Customers: Parker Hannifin, Eaton, Steris -> /about", "No minimum order quantity (MOQ) -> /", "24-hour lead times -> /", "Transparent tooling ownership and pricing -> /", "Direct access to engineers and leadership -> /about", "Regionally focused Midwest (OH, PA, MI, KY, WV) -> /about", "30+ years part design, 40+ years tool design experience -> /", "U.S.-based production in Northeast Ohio -> /", "Small project division for runs as low as 50 parts -> /about", "Engineering-led approach catching warpage, sink, assembly conflicts -> /services", "Reshoring support -> /services", "Tooling sourcing and management -> /services", "Assembly and secondary operations -> /services", "Additive and rapid prototyping support -> /services", "DFM/DFA guidance -> /services", "Tool refurbishment -> /services", "Prototyping, assembly, decoration, welding, packaging -> /services", "Flexible volume production -> /", "Family-owned accountability -> /about", "Ethical, transparent practices -> /about", "Customer-centric service -> /about", "Innovation with purpose -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "PharoPlast delivers engineering-led injection molding for companies that can''t afford rework.", "founded_year": "1972", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "No minimum order quantity", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/pharoplast/"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='pharoplast-injection-molding' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Phelps Industrial Products was established in 1945 in Laurel, Maryland, to supply fluid sealing products worldwide. The company operates as a manufacturer, fabricator, and distributor of industrial gaskets, compression packing, and sealing devices.

The company produces a range of sealing solutions including gaskets, compression packing, spiral wound gaskets, O-rings, molded parts, mechanical seals, marine products, adhesives, sealants, Topog-E boiler gaskets, and cutting tools. Its fabrication capabilities encompass die-cutting, laser-cutting, waterjet-cutting, and hand-cutting to meet custom requirements. Phelps serves a global customer base across North America, South America, Europe, Asia, the Middle East, and Australia.

