UPDATE companies SET description='Plas-Tech Tooling Inc. was founded in 1993 by Dean and Marcia Sonquist in Garner, Iowa. The business began in the couple’s garage, initially focused on injection mold building and repair for local manufacturers. By 1996 the operation had outgrown that space and moved to its current location in Garner, where it has expanded into a full-service machining and molding facility.

Today the company operates both a CNC machine shop and an injection molding department under one roof. Its machining lineup includes multiple Hurco vertical mills (VM10, VM30, VMX42, VMX50), Haas and Hurco lathes with live tooling and bar feeders, and a Puma 2600SYB II with opposing spindle. For molding, it runs a 300-ton JSW 280 ADS electric press and a 180-ton Sumitomo SH160 hydraulic press. Value‑added services include assembly, kitting, welding, inventory management, CAD drafting (SolidWorks, Mastercam), reverse engineering with a portable Hexagon CMM, and design‑for‑manufacturability feedback.

The shop serves a range of industries, with a noted focus on electronic‑industry fixturing using specialty plastics. It also supports startups and established OEMs that need rapid prototypes, emergency machining (including after‑hours response), or high‑volume “lights‑out” molding. Past work includes machining a critical part from solid bar stock when a casting supplier failed, delivering parts within weeks, and running high‑volume molding campaigns on electric presses.

Plas-Tech emphasizes the flexibility of a small company combined with the reliability and technology of a larger one. Its differentiators include in‑house tool design and build, no‑minimum‑quantity rapid machining, emergency machining with 24‑hour contact, and an ISO 9001:2015‑certified quality system that targets 100 % on‑time delivery and 100 % right‑first‑time components.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Production CNC machining (vertical mills, live-tooling lathes)", "Plastic injection molding (electric and hydraulic presses)", "Mold design and construction", "Rapid prototyping (no MOQ, no tooling costs)", "Emergency machining services", "Assembly, kitting, and welding", "Inventory management", "CAD/CAM drafting (SolidWorks, Mastercam)", "Reverse engineering with portable CMM", "Design for manufacturability feedback", "High-volume \u201clights-out\u201d molding", "Heat treatment (tool steel hardening)", "Sawing and surface grinding", "First article inspection and PPAP/ISIR documentation", "RoHS compliance certification"], "industries": ["Electronics"], "materials": ["Plastics", "Metals", "Tool Steel"], "equipment": ["Hurco VM 10", "Hurco VM30", "Hurco VMX42 (11 total)", "Hurco VMX50 (3 total)", "HAAS ST 30", "Hurco TMX8I", "Puma 2600SYB II (5 total)", "Hurco TMX10MYi (2 total)", "JSW 280 ADS (300 ton, 28 oz shot)", "Sumitomo SH 160 (180 ton, 7 oz shot)", "Grob Vertical Saw (18\u2033 throat)", "Do-All (12\u2033 diameter capacity)", "Master Cut Horizontal Saw (12\u2033 diameter capacity)", "Surface Grinder (2 total)", "Heat Treat (full tool steel hardening)", "Portable Hexagon Metrology Master 3D Gage (CMM)", "SOLIDWORKS", "Mastercam", "DrafSight"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Combined production machining and plastic injection molding in one facility", "No minimum order quantity for rapid machining and prototyping", "Emergency machining services with after-hours phone support", 